IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ltma-core`

-- Land Tax Management Act 1956 (NSW), read with the Land Tax Act 1956 (NSW) -- the owner's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the individual owner of land in New South Wales, including a joint owner and a foreign person liable to surcharge
-- land tax. "Do I owe land tax this year? Is my home exempt, including while I build, move or am away? How much do I owe,
-- alone or jointly? Must I lodge a return or make a family election, and by when? When must I pay, and do I get the
-- discount? As a foreign person, what surcharge do I owe, and can I keep my home exemption?" Every question is phrased as
-- that owner would ask it, on facts the owner could state. The rules are in ltma-core.l4; this module builds the core's
-- records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- EDITIONS: act-1956-026 and act-1956-027, NSW Legislation versions of 2 December 2024, from the Open Australian Legal
-- Corpus as collected on 10 March 2025. Not the current official text, and may be out of date. Thresholds for the 2025 and
-- later land tax years must be checked against the current register. Based on content from the New South Wales
-- Legislation website at 10 March 2025 (State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land tax -- the owner's questions`

-- Builds the core's record of a home from the answers every home question shares, and the owner's situation.
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `my situation`                                                          IS A `Use at the taxing date`
GIVETH A `Home at the taxing date`
`my home as the core records it` MEANS
    `Home at the taxing date` WITH
        `land tax year` IS `the land tax year I am asking about`
        `the land` IS
            `The land and its use` WITH
                `is a strata lot or strata lots`                                             IS `my home is a strata lot`
                `the building is designed, constructed or adapted for residential purposes` IS `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`
                `number of lots`                                                             IS `how many lots my home is on`
                `the lots adjoin`                                                            IS `the lots adjoin`
                `the lots are in the same ownership`                                         IS `the lots have the same owners`
                `the lots are a single residence`                                            IS `the lots are one single home`
                `there is a residential occupancy other than the owner's`                    IS `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`
                `that occupancy is one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`
                `that occupancy is on a lot the owner also lives on`                         IS `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`
                `one room is used primarily for a business conducted primarily elsewhere`   IS `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`
                `the land is used for another purpose or earns other income`                 IS `my home is used for something else or earns other income`
        `the use` IS `my situation`
        `a company owns or co-owns it, other than a trustee company or a trustee of a concessional trust` IS `a company owns or co-owns my home`
        `the owners who live there are owners only as trustees`                          IS `I own my home only as a trustee`
        `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns it`                                IS `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`
        `the family owns another residence one of them uses as a principal place of residence` IS `my family owns another home one of us lives in`
        `the family lodged an election in time`                                          IS `my family lodged an election in time`
        `the family elected this residence`                                              IS `my family elected this home`
        `this residence has the highest land value of the family's residences`           IS `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`
        `percentage owned by the owners who live there`                                  IS `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`
        `the owner is a participant in an approved shared equity scheme`                 IS `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`
        `the owner was previously entitled to the exemption for this land`               IS `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`

-- Builds the core's record of the owner's land for the land tax computation. One joint holding at most: the land owned
-- jointly with the same co-owners. A value of 0 means none.
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER
      `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home` IS A NUMBER
      `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners`  IS A NUMBER
      `my share of that jointly owned land`                                   IS A NUMBER
      `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Land owned at the taxing date`
`my land as the core records it` MEANS
    `Land owned at the taxing date` WITH
        `land tax year`                                              IS `the land tax year I am asking about`
        `average value of non-exempt land owned in severalty`        IS `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home`
        `joint holdings`                                             IS
            IF `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN LIST (`Joint holding` WITH `average value of the land held jointly` IS `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners`, `the owner's share` IS `my share of that jointly owned land`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `some of the land is subject to a special trust`             IS `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust`
        `a non-concessional company is an owner of some of the land` IS `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me`
        `the owner owns land only as a prescribed lessee`            IS `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner`

§§ `ss 8, 9AA, 62P and 62S -- when my land tax is fixed, and on what value`

@export On what day is my NSW land tax for this land tax year fixed, by what I own at midnight that day (s 8)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my land tax fixed` IS `the taxing date for` `the land tax year I am asking about`

@export What is the average value of my parcel of land for this NSW land tax year (s 9AA)?
GIVEN `the land value for this land tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The parcel's land value in the Valuer-General's Register as at 1 July of the year before this land tax year, in dollars
      `the land value for the previous land tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The parcel's land value as at 1 July two years before this land tax year, in dollars (0 if the parcel did not then exist)
      `the land value for the land tax year before that` IS A NUMBER @desc The parcel's land value as at 1 July three years before this land tax year, in dollars (0 if the parcel did not then exist)
      `how many of the 2 previous land tax years the parcel existed for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of the 2 previous land tax years the parcel existed on the 31 December before that year: 2, 1 or 0 (a newly created parcel)
      `any reduction or special allowance on my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Any land value reduction or special allowance (for example a subdivision allowance) that applies to the parcel this year, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the average value of my parcel` IS
    `the average value of`
        (`Parcel land values` WITH
            `land value for the current land tax year`                             IS `the land value for this land tax year`
            `land value for the preceding land tax year`                           IS `the land value for the previous land tax year`
            `land value for the land tax year before that`                         IS `the land value for the land tax year before that`
            `preceding land tax years before whose 31 December the parcel existed` IS `how many of the 2 previous land tax years the parcel existed for`
            `land value adjustment`                                                IS `any reduction or special allowance on my notice`)

@export What are the NSW land tax threshold and premium rate threshold for this land tax year (ss 62P, 62S)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026); years before 2009 are not covered
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Thresholds`
DECIDE `What are the land tax thresholds` IS `the thresholds for` `the land tax year I am asking about`

§§ `Schedule 1A -- is my home exempt?`

-- The 22 answers each home question shares come first, in the same order, so the form can ask them once.

@export Is my home exempt from NSW land tax as my principal place of residence, while I live in it (Schedule 1A cll 2-5, 11-15)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The land tax year, a calendar year; land tax for it is fixed by what you owned at midnight on the 31 December before
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your home is a strata lot (or 2 or more strata lots), such as an apartment or townhouse in a strata scheme
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is designed, built or adapted for people to live in (a house, rather than a shop or warehouse)
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many lots of land (or strata lots) your home is on; usually 1
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your home is on 2 or more lots: whether they adjoin (more than a shared corner point; strata lots sharing walls or floors; lots divided by a fence or wall only if there is ready access between them)
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your home is on 2 or more lots: whether the same person or the same joint owners own every lot
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your home is on 2 or more lots: whether they are the site of one single home (separate buildings that could be lived in separately do not count; strata lots need internal access between them)
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than you and your household occupies part of the property as a separate residence, such as a lodger, a boarder or a granny flat tenant
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it is only one of these -- one room; one suite of rooms (not a flat); one flat; one suite and one room; one flat and one room; or 2 separately occupied rooms
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your home is on 2 or more lots: whether that other occupancy is on a lot you also live on
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no more than one room is used mainly for a business, and that business is mainly conducted somewhere else
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any part of the land is used for something other than your home (beyond that one room or one other occupancy), or earns income from such a use
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company owns your home or is a co-owner (not counting a trustee company acting in its representative capacity, or a company acting as trustee of a concessional trust)
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every owner who lives there owns the home only as a trustee
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee of a special trust (a trust over land that is not a fixed trust, such as most discretionary trusts) owns or co-owns your home in that capacity
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, your spouse or de facto partner, or your dependent children under 18 who live with you, own another home that one of you lives in as a principal place of residence
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether your family lodged a written election of its principal place of residence within the objection period for the year's first notice of assessment
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family lodged an election: whether it elected this home
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family made no election: whether this home has the highest land value of your family's homes
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER  @desc The percentage of the home owned, together, by the owners who live there (100 if you own it all and live there)
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the home as a participant in a shared equity scheme approved under the Duties Act 1997, section 281
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to the principal place of residence exemption for this home in an earlier year (counts only up to the 2025 land tax year)
      `I have lived there continuously since 1 July last year, and in no other home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lived in this home, and no other, continuously since 1 July of the year before the land tax year, using it only as a home
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: whether the Chief Commissioner of State Revenue is satisfied that it is your principal place of residence (for example, you moved in after 1 July)
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is my home exempt while I live in it` IS
    `the principal place of residence exemption for`
        (`my home as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `my home is a strata lot` `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home` `how many lots my home is on` `the lots adjoin` `the lots have the same owners` `the lots are one single home` `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home` `that is just one excluded residential occupancy` `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on` `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else` `my home is used for something else or earns other income` `a company owns or co-owns my home` `I own my home only as a trustee` `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home` `my family owns another home one of us lives in` `my family lodged an election in time` `my family elected this home` `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes` `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there` `I am in an approved shared equity scheme` `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`
            (`the owner lives there` `I have lived there continuously since 1 July last year, and in no other home` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is my principal place of residence`))

-- Situation: the owner is building a home on land not yet lived in.
@export While I build my home on land I own, is the land exempt from NSW land tax (Schedule 1A cl 6)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The land tax year, a calendar year; land tax for it is fixed by what you owned at midnight on the 31 December before
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is a strata lot (or 2 or more strata lots)
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is already a building designed, built or adapted for people to live in (answer no for vacant land)
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many lots of land the home will be on; usually 1
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they adjoin (more than a shared corner point; lots divided by a fence or wall only if there is ready access between them)
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether the same person or the same joint owners own every lot
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they will be the site of one single home
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone else lives on the land in a separate residence (answer no for unoccupied land)
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it is only one room, one suite, one flat, a suite and a room, a flat and a room, or 2 separately occupied rooms
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether that occupancy is on a lot you also live on
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no more than one room is used mainly for a business conducted mainly elsewhere
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used for anything else, or earns income
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company owns the land or is a co-owner (not counting a trustee company acting in its representative capacity, or a company acting as trustee of a concessional trust)
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every owner who will live there owns the land only as a trustee
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns the land in that capacity
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, your spouse or de facto partner, or your dependent children under 18 who live with you, own another home one of you lives in
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether your family lodged a written election of its principal place of residence within the objection period
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family lodged an election: whether it elected this land
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family made no election: whether this land has the highest land value of your family's homes
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER  @desc The percentage of the land owned, together, by the owners who will live there (100 if you own it all)
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought as a participant in a shared equity scheme approved under the Duties Act 1997, section 281
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to the principal place of residence exemption for this land in an earlier year (counts only up to the 2025 land tax year)
      `the land is unoccupied`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is not being used or occupied for any purpose
      `I intend to live there solely as my principal place of residence`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live there, using it only as your principal place of residence
      `it is unoccupied because I intend to build or am building my home`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is unoccupied because you intend to carry out, or are carrying out, the building or other works needed to live there
      `the land has earned income since building work began`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any income has come from the land since the building work physically began
      `living there would be unlawful`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your intended use of the land as a home would be unlawful
      `the year I became the owner`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc The calendar year in which you became the owner of the land
      `someone else lived there after I bought it and before work began`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else lived on the land after you became the owner and before building work physically began
      `the year that person stopped living there`                             IS A NUMBER  @desc If so: the calendar year in which that person stopped living there
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied work began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone else lived there: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that, by the end of the first tax year of the period, building work began or significant steps were taken towards it
      `the number of tax years allowed for building`                          IS A NUMBER  @desc 4, unless the Chief Commissioner has extended the period because of exceptional delays beyond your control (then the extended number, at most 6)
      `my family or I have another home counted as a principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or a member of your family has another home whose actual use as a principal place of residence is being counted for land tax
      `I own a home outside NSW that is mine or my family's principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own land outside New South Wales that is the principal place of residence of you or a member of your family
      `more than 2 homes could lawfully be built on the land`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land (with any adjoining land you own) could lawfully have more than 2 homes or residential units built on it
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is my land exempt while I build my home` IS
    `the principal place of residence exemption for`
        (`my home as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `my home is a strata lot` `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home` `how many lots my home is on` `the lots adjoin` `the lots have the same owners` `the lots are one single home` `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home` `that is just one excluded residential occupancy` `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on` `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else` `my home is used for something else or earns other income` `a company owns or co-owns my home` `I own my home only as a trustee` `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home` `my family owns another home one of us lives in` `my family lodged an election in time` `my family elected this home` `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes` `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there` `I am in an approved shared equity scheme` `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`
            (`the owner is building a home there`
                (`Building facts` WITH
                    `the land is unoccupied`                                                         IS `the land is unoccupied`
                    `the owner intends to live there solely as principal place of residence`        IS `I intend to live there solely as my principal place of residence`
                    `it is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out or is carrying out the works` IS `it is unoccupied because I intend to build or am building my home`
                    `income has been derived since the works physically began`                       IS `the land has earned income since building work began`
                    `the intended use is unlawful`                                                   IS `living there would be unlawful`
                    `the year the owner became the owner`                                            IS `the year I became the owner`
                    `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`      IS `someone else lived there after I bought it and before work began`
                    `the year that person stopped living there`                                      IS `the year that person stopped living there`
                    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the works began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year` IS `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied work began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year`
                    `the period in tax years, as the Chief Commissioner has extended it`             IS `the number of tax years allowed for building`
                    `the owner or a family member has other land counted as a principal place of residence` IS `my family or I have another home counted as a principal place of residence`
                    `the owner owns land outside NSW that is the principal place of residence of the owner or a family member` IS `I own a home outside NSW that is mine or my family's principal place of residence`
                    `the land could lawfully have more than 2 residences built on it`                IS `more than 2 homes could lawfully be built on the land`)))

-- Situation: the owner owns an old and a new home at the same 31 December.
@export In the year I move, are both my former home and my new home exempt from NSW land tax (Schedule 1A cl 7)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The land tax year, a calendar year; land tax for it is fixed by what you owned at midnight on the 31 December before
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home you are asking about (former or new) is a strata lot (or 2 or more strata lots)
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home you are asking about is a building designed, built or adapted for people to live in
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many lots of land (or strata lots) that home is on; usually 1
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they adjoin (more than a shared corner point; strata lots sharing walls or floors)
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether the same person or the same joint owners own every lot
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they are the site of one single home
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than your household occupies part of that home as a separate residence
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it is only one room, one suite, one flat, a suite and a room, a flat and a room, or 2 separately occupied rooms
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether that occupancy is on a lot you also live on
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no more than one room is used mainly for a business conducted mainly elsewhere
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any part of that home is used for something other than a home, or earns income from such a use
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company owns that home or is a co-owner (not counting a trustee company acting in its representative capacity, or a company acting as trustee of a concessional trust)
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every owner who lives there owns it only as a trustee
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns that home in that capacity
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family owns a home other than your former and new homes that one of you lives in
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether your family lodged a written election of its principal place of residence within the objection period
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family lodged an election: whether it elected this home
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family made no election: whether this home has the highest land value of your family's homes
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER  @desc The percentage of that home owned, together, by the owners who live or will live there (100 if you own it all)
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought that home as a participant in a shared equity scheme approved under the Duties Act 1997, section 281
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to the principal place of residence exemption for that home in an earlier year (counts only up to the 2025 land tax year)
      `on the 31 December I owned both my former home and my new home`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at midnight on the 31 December before the land tax year, you owned both your former home and your new home
      `my former home was my principal place of residence on that 31 December or the one before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home was your principal place of residence on that 31 December, or on the 31 December a year earlier
      `I live in, or intend to live in, the new home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are living in, or intend to live in, the new home as your principal place of residence
      `since 1 July my former home has been only my home and earned no other income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since 1 July of that year, your former home was used only as your home and earned no income other than from one excluded occupancy or a lease to its buyer pending completion of the sale
      `the day I became the owner of my new home`                             IS A DATE    @desc The day you became the owner of the new home
      `since I bought it my new home has been used only as my home or by the previous owner's tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since you became its owner, the new home has been used only as your home or by a tenant under a lease the previous owner entered into
      `I already had both homes exempt this way on an earlier 31 December`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both these homes were already treated as your principal place of residence under this moving concession on an earlier 31 December
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Are both my homes exempt in the year I move` IS
    `the principal place of residence exemption for`
        (`my home as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `my home is a strata lot` `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home` `how many lots my home is on` `the lots adjoin` `the lots have the same owners` `the lots are one single home` `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home` `that is just one excluded residential occupancy` `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on` `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else` `my home is used for something else or earns other income` `a company owns or co-owns my home` `I own my home only as a trustee` `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home` `my family owns another home one of us lives in` `my family lodged an election in time` `my family elected this home` `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes` `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there` `I am in an approved shared equity scheme` `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`
            (`the owner is moving home`
                (`Moving facts` WITH
                    `the owner owns both a former residence and a new residence`                     IS `on the 31 December I owned both my former home and my new home`
                    `the former residence was the owner's principal place of residence on this or the preceding taxing date` IS `my former home was my principal place of residence on that 31 December or the one before`
                    `the new residence is being or is intended to be the owner's principal place of residence` IS `I live in, or intend to live in, the new home as my principal place of residence`
                    `the former residence was used only as the owner's home, without other income, since the preceding 1 July` IS `since 1 July my former home has been only my home and earned no other income`
                    `the day the owner became the owner of the new residence`                        IS `the day I became the owner of my new home`
                    `the new residence was used only as the owner's home or by a tenant of the previous owner` IS `since I bought it my new home has been used only as my home or by the previous owner's tenant`
                    `both residences were already exempt under clause 7 on an earlier taxing date`  IS `I already had both homes exempt this way on an earlier 31 December`)))

-- Situation: the owner has moved out of a former home.
@export While I am living away from my former home, is it still exempt from NSW land tax (Schedule 1A cl 8)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The land tax year, a calendar year; land tax for it is fixed by what you owned at midnight on the 31 December before
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home is a strata lot (or 2 or more strata lots)
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home is a building designed, built or adapted for people to live in
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many lots of land (or strata lots) your former home is on; usually 1
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they adjoin (more than a shared corner point; strata lots sharing walls or floors)
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether the same person or the same joint owners own every lot
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they are the site of one single home
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from any letting of the whole home, anyone occupies part of it as a separate residence
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it is only one room, one suite, one flat, a suite and a room, a flat and a room, or 2 separately occupied rooms
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether that occupancy is on a lot that was your home
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no more than one room is used mainly for a business conducted mainly elsewhere
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any part of the land is used for something other than a home
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company owns your former home or is a co-owner (not counting a trustee company acting in its representative capacity, or a company acting as trustee of a concessional trust)
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every owner who is treated as living there owns it only as a trustee
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns your former home in that capacity
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, your spouse or de facto partner, or your dependent children under 18 who live with you, own another home one of you lives in as a principal place of residence
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether your family lodged a written election of its principal place of residence within the objection period
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family lodged an election: whether it elected this former home
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your family made no election: whether this former home has the highest land value of your family's homes
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER  @desc The percentage of the home owned, together, by the owners who are treated as living there (100 if you own it all)
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the home as a participant in a shared equity scheme approved under the Duties Act 1997, section 281
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to the principal place of residence exemption for this home in an earlier year (counts only up to the 2025 land tax year)
      `I lived there as my principal place of residence for at least 6 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived in the home as your principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months before you left
      `I own other land I live in as my principal place of residence`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now own other land that you live in as your principal place of residence
      `the day I stopped living there`                                        IS A DATE    @desc The day your last period (of at least 6 months) of actually living there ended
      `days I have spent in full time care since then`                        IS A NUMBER  @desc Days since then you have spent in full time care: as a hospital patient, in residential or respite aged care, or living with a carer who is eligible for carer payment under the Social Security Act 1991 for caring for you
      `the home earned income in the year before the land tax year`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any income came from the home (for example rent) in the calendar year before the land tax year
      `a single letting that year ran for more than 6 months`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether any one lease, licence or other right to occupy ran for a continuous period of more than 6 months in that year
      `the days the home was let that year`                                   IS A NUMBER  @desc If so: the total days in that year for which someone had a right to occupy the home for income (each overnight stay counts as one day)
      `the income only covered rates, charges and maintenance`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the income was no more than reasonably needed to cover council, water and energy rates and charges and maintenance costs
      `the home has been unfit to live in for more than 4 years`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has been incapable of being used as a residence for a period of more than 4 years
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is my former home still exempt while I am away` IS
    `the principal place of residence exemption for`
        (`my home as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `my home is a strata lot` `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home` `how many lots my home is on` `the lots adjoin` `the lots have the same owners` `the lots are one single home` `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home` `that is just one excluded residential occupancy` `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on` `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else` `my home is used for something else or earns other income` `a company owns or co-owns my home` `I own my home only as a trustee` `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home` `my family owns another home one of us lives in` `my family lodged an election in time` `my family elected this home` `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes` `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there` `I am in an approved shared equity scheme` `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`
            (`the owner is away`
                (`Absence facts` WITH
                    `the owner lived there as principal place of residence continuously for at least 6 months` IS `I lived there as my principal place of residence for at least 6 months in a row`
                    `the owner owns other land the owner lives in as principal place of residence` IS `I own other land I live in as my principal place of residence`
                    `the day the owner stopped living there`                                         IS `the day I stopped living there`
                    `days in full time care since then`                                              IS `days I have spent in full time care since then`
                    `income was derived from the land in the preceding tax year`                     IS `the home earned income in the year before the land tax year`
                    `a right of occupation in that year ran continuously for more than 6 months`     IS `a single letting that year ran for more than 6 months`
                    `days of occupation let in that year`                                            IS `the days the home was let that year`
                    `the income was no more than rates, charges and maintenance costs`               IS `the income only covered rates, charges and maintenance`
                    `the land has been incapable of being used as a residence for more than 4 years` IS `the home has been unfit to live in for more than 4 years`)))

-- Situation: the owner who lived in the home has died; asked by the personal representative or a beneficiary.
@export After the owner who lived in a home has died, is it still exempt from NSW land tax (Schedule 1A cl 9)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about`                                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The land tax year, a calendar year; land tax for it is fixed by what was owned at midnight on the 31 December before
      `my home is a strata lot`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is a strata lot (or 2 or more strata lots)
      `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is a building designed, built or adapted for people to live in
      `how many lots my home is on`                                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many lots of land (or strata lots) the home is on; usually 1
      `the lots adjoin`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they adjoin (more than a shared corner point; strata lots sharing walls or floors)
      `the lots have the same owners`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether the same person or the same joint owners own every lot
      `the lots are one single home`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether they are the site of one single home
      `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone occupied part of the home as a separate residence
      `that is just one excluded residential occupancy`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it is only one room, one suite, one flat, a suite and a room, a flat and a room, or 2 separately occupied rooms
      `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If 2 or more lots: whether that occupancy was on a lot the owner lived on
      `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no more than one room was used mainly for a business conducted mainly elsewhere
      `my home is used for something else or earns other income`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any part of the land is used for something other than a home
      `a company owns or co-owns my home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company owned the home or was a co-owner before the death (not counting a trustee company acting in its representative capacity)
      `I own my home only as a trustee`                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner who lived there owned it only as a trustee
      `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee of a special trust owned or co-owned the home in that capacity
      `my family owns another home one of us lives in`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner's family (spouse or de facto partner, and dependent children under 18 living with them) owned another home one of them lived in
      `my family lodged an election in time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the family lodged a written election of its principal place of residence within the objection period
      `my family elected this home`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the family lodged an election: whether it elected this home
      `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc If no election was made: whether this home has the highest land value of the family's homes
      `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there`         IS A NUMBER  @desc The percentage of the home the owner who died owned, with any co-owners who lived there (100 if the owner owned it all)
      `I am in an approved shared equity scheme`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner bought as a participant in a shared equity scheme approved under the Duties Act 1997, section 281
      `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner was entitled to the principal place of residence exemption for this home in an earlier year (counts only up to the 2025 land tax year)
      `immediately before death the owner owned the home and lived there as principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before death, the person who died owned the home and lived in it as their principal place of residence
      `the day the owner died`                                                IS A DATE    @desc The day the owner died
      `the home has been transferred to someone other than the executor or a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the 31 December before the land tax year, the home had been transferred to anyone other than the personal representative or a beneficiary of the estate
      `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has extended (in writing, and not withdrawn) the 2-year period after the death
      `the day the extended period ends`                                      IS A DATE    @desc If so: the day the extended period ends
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is the home of the owner who died still exempt` IS
    `the principal place of residence exemption for`
        (`my home as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `my home is a strata lot` `my home is a building designed, built or adapted as a home` `how many lots my home is on` `the lots adjoin` `the lots have the same owners` `the lots are one single home` `someone else has a separate residential occupancy in my home` `that is just one excluded residential occupancy` `that occupancy is on a lot I also live on` `I use one room mainly for a business I run mainly somewhere else` `my home is used for something else or earns other income` `a company owns or co-owns my home` `I own my home only as a trustee` `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns my home` `my family owns another home one of us lives in` `my family lodged an election in time` `my family elected this home` `this home has the highest land value of my family's homes` `the percentage of my home owned by those of us who live there` `I am in an approved shared equity scheme` `I was entitled to the exemption for this home before`
            (`the owner has died`
                (`Death facts` WITH
                    `immediately before death the owner owned the land and lived there as principal place of residence` IS `immediately before death the owner owned the home and lived there as principal place of residence`
                    `the day the owner died`                                                         IS `the day the owner died`
                    `the land has been transferred to someone other than the personal representative or a beneficiary` IS `the home has been transferred to someone other than the executor or a beneficiary`
                    `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`                     IS `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`
                    `the day the extended period ends`                                               IS `the day the extended period ends`)))

-- Situation: the owner is building (cl 6(5)).
@export While I build my home, by what date must I move in to keep the NSW land tax exemption (Schedule 1A cl 6(3), (5), (7A))?
GIVEN `the year I became the owner of the land`                     IS A NUMBER  @desc The calendar year in which you became the owner of the land
      `someone else lived on the land after I bought it`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else lived on the land after you became the owner and before building work physically began
      `the year that person moved out`                               IS A NUMBER  @desc If so: the calendar year in which that person stopped living there
      `the tax years allowed for building`                           IS A NUMBER  @desc 4, unless the Chief Commissioner has extended the period because of exceptional delays beyond your control (then the extended number, at most 6)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I move into the home I am building` IS
    `the end of the clause 6 period`
        (`Building facts` WITH
            `the land is unoccupied`                                                         IS TRUE   -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the owner intends to live there solely as principal place of residence`        IS TRUE   -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `it is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out or is carrying out the works` IS TRUE   -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `income has been derived since the works physically began`                       IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the intended use is unlawful`                                                   IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the year the owner became the owner`                                            IS `the year I became the owner of the land`
            `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`      IS `someone else lived on the land after I bought it`
            `the year that person stopped living there`                                      IS `the year that person moved out`
            `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the works began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year` IS TRUE   -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the period in tax years, as the Chief Commissioner has extended it`             IS `the tax years allowed for building`
            `the owner or a family member has other land counted as a principal place of residence` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the owner owns land outside NSW that is the principal place of residence of the owner or a family member` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the land could lawfully have more than 2 residences built on it`                IS FALSE) -- placeholder: no rule here reads it

@export Once I move into the home I built, until what date must I keep living there to keep the NSW land tax exemption (Schedule 1A cl 6(5))?
GIVEN `the day I moved in` IS A DATE @desc The day you actually began living in the home as your principal place of residence
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what date must I keep living in the home I built` IS `months after` `the day I moved in` 6

-- Situation: the owner is moving (cl 7(3A)).
@export If both my former and new homes were exempt in the year I moved, by what date must I be living in the new home (Schedule 1A cl 7(3A))?
GIVEN `the land tax year both homes were exempt for` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year for which both homes were treated as your principal place of residence
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I be living in my new home` IS `the next taxing date after the one for` `the land tax year both homes were exempt for`

-- Situation: the owner is away (cl 8(2), (4)).
@export While I am away from my former home, until what date can it still be treated as my home for NSW land tax (Schedule 1A cl 8(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the day I stopped living there`             IS A DATE   @desc The day your last period (of at least 6 months) of actually living there ended
      `days I have spent in full time care since then` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since then you have spent in full time care: as a hospital patient, in residential or respite aged care, or living with a carer who is eligible for carer payment under the Social Security Act 1991 for caring for you
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what date can my former home be treated as my home` IS
    `the end of the clause 8 period`
        (`Absence facts` WITH
            `the owner lived there as principal place of residence continuously for at least 6 months` IS TRUE   -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the owner owns other land the owner lives in as principal place of residence` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the day the owner stopped living there`                                         IS `the day I stopped living there`
            `days in full time care since then`                                              IS `days I have spent in full time care since then`
            `income was derived from the land in the preceding tax year`                     IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `a right of occupation in that year ran continuously for more than 6 months`     IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `days of occupation let in that year`                                            IS 0      -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the income was no more than rates, charges and maintenance costs`               IS FALSE  -- placeholder: no rule here reads it
            `the land has been incapable of being used as a residence for more than 4 years` IS FALSE) -- placeholder: no rule here reads it

§§ `Schedule 1A cl 12 -- one home for the whole family`

-- Situation: the family (spouses or de facto partners, and dependent children) owns more than one home one of them lives in.
@export My family owns more than one home we live in: by what date must we lodge our election of one as our principal place of residence (Schedule 1A cl 12(3)-(4))?
GIVEN `the day the first notice of assessment for the year was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the initial notice of assessment of land tax for the year was served on you
      `days allowed for an objection` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Taxation Administration Act 1996, section 89, allows for lodging an objection to that notice (not in this encoding; check the Act)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my family lodge its election` IS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day the first notice of assessment for the year was served` PLUS `days allowed for an objection`)

§§ `ss 9 and 27; Land Tax Act Schedule 13 -- how much land tax do I owe?`

@export How much NSW land tax do I owe for this land tax year, on the land I own alone and the land I own jointly (s 27; Land Tax Act s 3AL, Schedule 13 Part 1)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026); years before 2009 are not covered
      `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the average values (see the average value question) of every parcel you owned alone at midnight on the 31 December before, leaving out your exempt home and any other exempt land, in dollars
      `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the average values of the whole of the land you own jointly or in common with the same co-owners, leaving out an exempt home, in dollars; 0 if none
      `my share of that jointly owned land` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of that jointly owned land, as a fraction (one half is 0.5)
      `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold any of this land as trustee of a special trust (a trust over land that is not a fixed trust, such as most discretionary trusts)
      `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company classified as a non-concessional company (one of a group of related companies) is a co-owner of any of this land
      `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold any of this land only under a lease, as a lessee the regulations treat as its owner
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Land tax assessed`
DECIDE `How much land tax do I owe` IS
    `the land tax assessed on` (`my land as the core records it` `the land tax year I am asking about` `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home` `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners` `my share of that jointly owned land` `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust` `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me` `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner`)

@export Do I owe any NSW land tax for this land tax year, alone or jointly (ss 7, 9, 27; Land Tax Act Schedule 13 Part 1)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026); years before 2009 are not covered
      `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the average values of every parcel you owned alone at midnight on the 31 December before, leaving out your exempt home and any other exempt land, in dollars
      `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the average values of the whole of the land you own jointly or in common with the same co-owners, leaving out an exempt home, in dollars; 0 if none
      `my share of that jointly owned land` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of that jointly owned land, as a fraction (one half is 0.5)
      `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold any of this land as trustee of a special trust
      `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a company classified as a non-concessional company is a co-owner of any of this land
      `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold any of this land only under a lease, as a lessee the regulations treat as its owner
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I owe any land tax` IS
    CONSIDER `How much land tax do I owe` `the land tax year I am asking about` `the total average value of the land I own alone, leaving out my exempt home` `the average value of the land I own jointly with the same co-owners` `my share of that jointly owned land` `I own some of the land as trustee of a special trust` `a non-concessional company owns some of the land with me` `I hold some of the land only as a lessee the regulations make an owner`
    WHEN `answered` `the amounts` THEN `answered` (`the amounts`'s `payable on the separate assessment` GREATER THAN 0 OR `the amounts`'s `payable on the joint assessments` GREATER THAN 0)
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

§§ `ss 12, 39 and 40 -- returns and payment`

DECLARE `Return answer` IS ONE OF
    `I must lodge a land tax return` HAS
        `by`                         IS A DATE
        `listing all land I owned at midnight on` IS A DATE
    `no Gazette order requires me to lodge a return for the year, though the Chief Commissioner may ask for one under s 12(2)`

@export Must I lodge a NSW land tax return for this year, and by what date (s 12(1A)-(1B))?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026)
      `a Gazette order requires people like me to lodge a return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order of the Chief Commissioner published in the Gazette under s 12(1) requires you, or a class of persons you belong to, to lodge a land tax return for the year
GIVETH A `Return answer`
DECIDE `Must I lodge a land tax return` IS
    IF `a Gazette order requires people like me to lodge a return for the year`
    THEN `I must lodge a land tax return` (`the s 12(1A) return date for` `the land tax year I am asking about`) (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year I am asking about`)
    ELSE `no Gazette order requires me to lodge a return for the year, though the Chief Commissioner may ask for one under s 12(2)`

@export By what date must I pay the NSW land tax in my notice of assessment (s 39(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of assessment was served on you
      `the due date in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date by which the notice says the land tax is to be paid
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I pay my land tax` IS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` PLUS `days from service to the day land tax must be paid` (`days from` `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` `to` `the due date in the notice`))

@export Do I get the NSW land tax early payment discount, and how much is it (s 40)?
GIVEN `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of assessment was served on you
      `the day I paid` IS A DATE @desc The day you paid
      `I paid the whole amount in the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the whole amount the assessment specifies
      `I owed no other land tax, interest or penalty tax, or paid it all at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you paid, you owed the Chief Commissioner no other land tax, interest or penalty tax (even if disputed), or paid all of it with this payment
      `the land tax in the assessment, leaving out overdue land tax` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax the assessment specifies, leaving out any overdue land tax, in dollars
      `the discount rate the Treasurer has ordered, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The discount rate set by the Treasurer's order published in the Gazette for the assessment, as a percentage (not in this encoding; check the current order)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What early payment discount do I get` IS
    IF `the s 40 discount is earned` (`days from` `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` `to` `the day I paid`) `I paid the whole amount in the assessment` `I owed no other land tax, interest or penalty tax, or paid it all at the same time`
    THEN `the s 40 discount on` `the land tax in the assessment, leaving out overdue land tax` (`the discount rate the Treasurer has ordered, as a percentage` DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0

§§ `Land Tax Act ss 5A and 5B -- surcharge land tax for a foreign person`

-- Situation: the owner is a foreign person (Duties Act 1997 Chapter 2A) who owns residential land.

@export As a foreign person, how much NSW surcharge land tax do I owe for this land tax year (Land Tax Act s 5A)?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026)
      `I am a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a foreign person within the meaning of Chapter 2A of the Duties Act 1997 (in general, not an Australian citizen, and not ordinarily resident in Australia)
      `the value of my interests in residential land, leaving out a home exempt from surcharge` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, over the residential land you owned at midnight on the 31 December before, of your share of each parcel's average value, leaving out a home exempt from surcharge land tax, in dollars
      `some of that land is used for other than residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that some of that residential land is used for purposes other than residential purposes
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` IS
    `the surcharge land tax on`
        (`Residential land of a foreign person` WITH
            `land tax year` IS `the land tax year I am asking about`
            `the owner is a foreign person` IS `I am a foreign person`
            `the value of the owner's interests in residential land not exempt from surcharge` IS `the value of my interests in residential land, leaving out a home exempt from surcharge`
            `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied some of it is used for other than residential purposes` IS `some of that land is used for other than residential purposes`)

@export As a foreign person, is my home exempt from NSW surcharge land tax (Land Tax Act s 5A(4)(g), s 5B(1))?
GIVEN `my home is exempt from land tax as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your home is exempt from ordinary land tax under the principal place of residence exemption (see the home questions)
      `I was a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian permanent resident at midnight on the 31 December before the land tax year
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied I intend to live there 200 continuous days this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that, during the land tax year, you intend to live in the home as your principal place of residence for a continuous period of 200 days
      `I lodged the declaration of that intention with a land tax return I was required to lodge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a declaration of that intention with a land tax return required under s 12 of the Land Tax Management Act 1956 for the year
      `I am a retirement visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a retirement visa within the meaning of Chapter 2A of the Duties Act 1997
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` IS
    `the s 5B(1) eligibility of`
        (`Surcharge home facts` WITH
            `the home is exempt under the principal place of residence exemption` IS `my home is exempt from land tax as my principal place of residence`
            `the person was a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the previous year` IS `I was a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the previous year`
            `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the person intends to meet the residence requirement` IS `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied I intend to live there 200 continuous days this year`
            `the person lodged the declaration with a land tax return required under s 12` IS `I lodged the declaration of that intention with a land tax return I was required to lodge`
            `the person is a retirement visa holder` IS `I am a retirement visa holder`)

@export As a foreign person whose home is exempt from surcharge, by what date must I start living there to complete 200 continuous days this year (Land Tax Act s 5B(2))?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I start my 200 days` IS `the latest day to begin the s 5B(2) period in` `the land tax year I am asking about`

@export As a foreign person, did I meet the 200-day residence requirement for my home this year (Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(2A))?
GIVEN `the land tax year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax year, a calendar year (for example 2026)
      `the first day of my longest stretch living there` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your longest unbroken stretch in the land tax year living in the home as your principal place of residence, without leaving Australia (unless the Chief Commissioner waived a brief absence)
      `the last day of that stretch` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that stretch
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` IS
    `the residence requirement is met by` `the land tax year I am asking about` `the first day of my longest stretch living there` `the last day of that stretch`
